  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 212 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nDry weather continues to be expected through the workweek. A\nbroad area of high pressure moves through the Ohio River Valley\ntoday and tomorrow, with an upper ridge axis moving through\nTuesday. Highs generally in the 70s are forecast both days with\nlows in the upper 40s to near 50. Afterwards, southerly flow\nbrings in warmer air midweek with highs Wednesday rising to the\n80s. A weak, dry boundary Wednesday brings a wind shift but\nrising 500mb heights and a subsequent high pressure area moving\nthrough keeps temperatures above normal for the remainder of the\nweek.\n\nPoPs over the weekend remain fairly steady, around 20-35% south\nof the Ohio River Saturday night into Sunday. Models still\ndiffer on the focus for this system, with an upper low over the\nRio Grande and the remnants of a tropical system among possible\ncontributors. Areas south/southeast of the Quad State will have\nhigher precipitation potential. Positioning of high pressure \noff the Mid-Atlantic will influence how far northwestward in the\nQuad State precipitation is able to reach.",
